From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Henrik Klee <henrik@goat-code.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 22:35:32 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Input: apple_z2: Start a D21 with the working configuration's
 last write

The D21 boot wrote 0x10003458 = 1 after the calibration and 6 to
0x10003058. The working configuration (d21-touch.service gold line,
corrected 2026-11-03 from D21.mtprops) writes 3 to 0x10003058 and ends
with 0x10003400 = 1. Without that write the firmware loads, answers the
first kick and never starts scanning; since the core rail is cut before
every power-up, every start is a cold one and stays dead.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/input/touchscreen/apple_z2.c | 9 +++++----
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/input/touchscreen/apple_z2.c b/drivers/input/touchscreen/apple_z2.c
index fa03abfa4..8fb33b202 100644
--- a/drivers/input/touchscreen/apple_z2.c
+++ b/drivers/input/touchscreen/apple_z2.c
@@ -4861,19 +4861,20 @@ static const struct apple_z2_chip_info apple_z2_d111_info = {
 /*
  * iPhone 8 Plus (D21), personality C1F5E,4 of D21.mtprops: the iPhone 7
  * Plus boot and report layout with the generation-1 data phase. @regs are
- * the personality's boot sequence; 0x10003458 after the calibration is the
- * write of the tested configuration.
+ * the boot sequence of the working configuration (DUGS's d21-touch.service
+ * gold line): five writes, the calibration, then 0x10003400 = 1, which
+ * starts the controller. Without it a cold-booted D21 never scans.
  */
 static const struct apple_z2_hbpp_reg apple_z2_d21_regs[] = {
 	{ 0x10003060, 0x17d3 },	/* fll-mval */
 	{ 0x1000305c, 2 },	/* reference clock divider */
-	{ 0x10003058, 6 },
+	{ 0x10003058, 3 },
 	{ 0x10003000, 3 },
 	{ 0x10003518, 1 },	/* clk32-clock-enable */
 };
 
 static const struct apple_z2_hbpp_reg apple_z2_d21_post_cal_regs[] = {
-	{ 0x10003458, 1 },
+	{ 0x10003400, 1 },
 };
 
